# arx-pub-db / community.db — the arx community registry (PUBLIC, unofficial)
#
# Community-contributed PUBLIC git repositories that arx can browse and install. Anyone can add
# a repo by opening a pull request against this file. This is the open, community half of arx:
# the official, signed, R2-delivered tools live in arx's tools index (fetched + sha256-verified),
# NOT here. Entries here are NOT vetted or signed by Stingray Labs — arx builds/installs them
# straight from their public git source, so treat them like the AUR: read the code, install at
# your own risk. arx still runs its normal pre-exec guard + PKGBUILD/script scan on them.
#
# Format — pipe-delimited, one repo per line, exactly 5 fields, no trailing pipe:
#   name | repo_url | category | description | maintainer
#
#   name        unique, [a-z0-9-] (becomes the arx install target + clone dir)
#   repo_url    an https:// git URL (HTTPS only — arx refuses ssh/file/http)
#   category    tool | theme | plugin | arsenal | kernel | lib | other
#   description one short line, no pipes
#   maintainer  the contributor's GitHub handle (who vouches for / maintains the entry)
#
# Install one with:  arx pub install <name>       Browse:  arx pub            (see the README)
# Lines starting with # are comments; blank lines are ignored.
#
kernel-builder|https://github.com/0xb0rn3/kernel-builder|tool|arx Kernel Tuner (akt): cross-distro kernel build with a config gate + web GUI|0xb0rn3
deathstr0ke|https://github.com/0xb0rn3/deathstr0ke|tool|Emergency anti-forensics: duress crypto-erase, pre-boot LUKS hook, PAM trigger|0xb0rn3
